diff --git a/docs/spec/CODEGEN_SPEC.md b/docs/spec/CODEGEN_SPEC.md
--- a/docs/spec/CODEGEN_SPEC.md
+++ b/docs/spec/CODEGEN_SPEC.md
@@ -57,7 +57,18 @@
 - An island is made for each connected component of the graph. `ff` and `ff-plain` processes woken by the same trigger (a slot, its bits and an edge) go into one island.
 - The level order is a topological order of the graph; ties are broken by SIR process number. The same SIR and the same options give the same table, byte for byte.
 - On both tiers, eligible strongly connected components iterate until they settle, up to `--max-scc-iter` (UNSPECIFIED_BEHAVIOR.md A6, CLI.md 2.6).
-- No slot is removed or merged: every slot keeps its storage.
+- Preserve slot identity and storage for the ordinary path. A fused
+  region may keep an intermediate in a local value only after proving
+  all readers, writers, observers and aliases.
+- Slots preserved for waveform, foreign access, force or explicit
+  reasons, including `--preserve` and `--public`, retain their writes
+  at the original points. Materialize any needed values through the
+  completed logical prefix before an observation, interrupt, callback
+  or exit. Use ordinary stores when materialization cannot be proved.
+- Compare logical writes and PerfCount including omitted physical
+  stores in `--tier-check`. Include the verified analysis, ABI
+  capability and layout in the cache. Use ordinary slot storage
+  on unknown capability or analysis.
 - A missing or stale entry of the analysis table means unknown (the SIR v1 proposal, D6), and such a process stays out of islands (`unknown-entry`).

 ### Island execution on tier 1
diff --git a/docs/spec/CODEGEN_SPEC.ja.md b/docs/spec/CODEGEN_SPEC.ja.md
